{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SuffixAutomaton","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is built one symbol at a time in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected steps, with at most 2"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" − 1 states and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"3"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" − 4 transitions. Each state stands for the substrings that end at the same set of places"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the text; its suffix link leads to the state of the longest of their suffixes that ends at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more places. A pattern is checked in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":") transitions."}]},{"code":["let automaton = SuffixAutomaton(\"abcbc\")","automaton.contains(\"cbc\")              \/\/ true","automaton.occurrenceCount(of: \"bc\")    \/\/ 2","automaton.firstOccurrence(of: \"cb\")    \/\/ 2 ..< 4","automaton.distinctSubstringCount       \/\/ 12","automaton.longestCommonSubstring(with: \"xbcbz\")?.textRange  